; lisp: float-round-trip.lisp
; The whole sample of float-round-trip (cases/float-round-trip.cases), run
; only when named, about 8 minutes on micro.
; Every float prints, and its printed text reads back as the same float, bit
; for bit (sys/io/print.lisp, PRINT-FLONUM; sys/io/read.lisp,
; XR-FLONUM-CONS; lisp/float-round-trip.lisp).  SI:FRT-RUN round trips a
; sample of floats of one format, short or single, and gives the number that
; did not come back, the number tried, and up to three of them: the text, the
; float's exact value as (M E), M * 2^E, and what the text read back as or
; the error.  The samples are built from bits and exact integers, not by the
; reader: the extremes of both signs, the constants as the system has them,
; and the floats the faults were found with (6.02e23, 2^-20 and 2^-127
; short, the float just above 2^-1024, 1e-307); 2^k of both signs for every
; k in range, and the floats on each side of it for every eighth k and the
; ends; the floats nearest 10^k of both signs for every k in range; and 3000
; pseudo-random floats of every exponent and sign from a seeded LCG.
; The printer scaled a float outside [1e-3, 1e7) to [1, 10) by floating
; multiplication, losing bits, and printed the scaled float's digits; the
; reader multiplied or divided by a floating power of ten, losing bits
; again, read a short float as a single one and rounded that, and negated
; the magnitude it read, so that -2^1023 and -2^127, whose magnitudes are no
; floats, overflowed.
; Run with --compile --files sys/io/print.lisp,sys/io/read.lisp,
; tools/system-check/lisp/float-round-trip.lisp on a band built before the
; change.
(si:frt-run :short :extremes) => (0 17)
(si:frt-run :short :powers-of-2) => (0 682)
(si:frt-run :short :powers-of-10) => (0 154)
(si:frt-run :short :random) => (0 3000)
(si:frt-run :single :extremes) => (0 15)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 0 500) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 500 1000) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 1000 1500) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 1500 2000) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 2000 2500) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 2500 3000) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 3000 3500) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 3500 4000) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 4000 4500) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 4500 5000) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-2 5000 5500) => (0 162)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-10 0 500) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-10 500 1000) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :powers-of-10 1000 1500) => (0 232)
(si:frt-run :single :random 0 500) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :random 500 1000) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :random 1000 1500) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :random 1500 2000) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :random 2000 2500) => (0 500)
(si:frt-run :single :random 2500 3000) => (0 500)
